  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 353 AM MDT THU JUL 23 2026\nThe pattern through the extended will be very similar to late \nthis week, but more moderated with slow day-to-day changes. An \nupper level trough along/off the coast and upper level ridging \nto our east will continue dry southwest flow across the area. \nTemperatures will remain hot, although slightly cooler thanks to\nthe trough with lower valleys reaching the mid 90s. \nTemperatures may increase several degrees by the end of the \nperiod as the ridge builds back to the west. Winds will remain \nbreezy, but not as strong as Saturday due to a weaker pressure \ngradient. Dry air will keep shower and thunderstorm chances \nminimal, but will tick up across south-central Idaho to 10-20% \nby mid to late week as the ridge expands and allows monsoonal \nmoisture back into eastern areas.",
